You are an expert Next.js 16, React 19, and Tailwind developer.
Always use the App Router (src/app).

Before any task, read and follow:
- context/ai-interaction.md (mandatory workflow, branching, commit policy)
- context/coding-standards.md (mandatory engineering conventions)
- context/project-overview.md (product scope and data model)
- context/current-feature.md (work in flight; update it as you work)

Always refer to docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for data models and folder structure before generating code.
UI and styling decisions must follow UI_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md and the tokens in src/app/globals.css.

We are using Prisma (v7 + @prisma/adapter-pg) as our ORM and Clerk for authentication.
Never use client-side state (like Zustand or Redux) for database data; always prefer React Server Components and Server Actions.
Do not commit or push without permission. Verify with `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, and `npm run build` before claiming work is done.
